<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<databaseChangeLog
        xmlns="http://www.liquibase.org/xml/ns/dbchangelog"
        xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance"
        xsi:schemaLocation="http://www.liquibase.org/xml/ns/dbchangelog
        http://www.liquibase.org/xml/ns/dbchangelog/dbchangelog-latest.xsd">

    <!-- SCRUM-91: man_ext_status was projection-dressing over the MSR-written mandate
         table (SELECT DISTINCT ... FROM mandate JOIN the spine), not the specified
         consolidation view. mnd_ext_status (004) plus mandate_effective_status (005)
         supersede it, and ManWatermarkRepo now reads the latter.

         ORDERED FIRST IN THE MASTER as of SCRUM-91, ahead of the shared-core bootstrap, and
         that position is load-bearing. 000 now carries the same un-cascaded guarded drop of
         the `mandate` projection that all ten M-services carry, and CockroachDB refuses an
         un-cascaded drop while a view still selects from the table. A database migrated by a
         jar built between 003 and this changeset still carries the view, so retiring it
         BEFORE the shared core runs is what lets that state converge instead of failing every
         migration MRG attempts. Nothing reads the view when it goes: 004/005 and the
         re-pointed ManWatermarkRepo shipped in the same wave, and MRG's delta has read
         mandate_current_status since.

         The include position is how this is ordered, NOT a rename: changeset identity is
         (id, author, FILENAME), so renaming the file would re-run it as a new changeset.

         The viewExists guard is what makes every reachable DB state converge: a fresh
         database never creates man_ext_status at all (SCRUM-91 removed the 003 changeset that
         built it), and a re-run finds it gone and MARK_RANs. -->
    <changeSet id="006-drop-man-ext-status" author="dcre">
        <preConditions onFail="MARK_RAN"><viewExists viewName="man_ext_status"/></preConditions>
        <dropView viewName="man_ext_status"/>
    </changeSet>

</databaseChangeLog>
